  "title": "Iqa‘ Hacha‘ 4/4",
  "subtitle": "(also in 2/4 and 6/4)",
  "description": "Iqa‘ Hacha‘",
  "lang": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    "Iqa‘ Hacha‘ in 4/4 is very popular in Sufi music, especially in pieces that only use percussion instruments. Although the 4/4 version is by far the most prevalent, it is an adaptation of a more folkloric iqa‘ by the same name in 2/4. A rare adaptation is the 6/4 version used by composer Baligh Hamdi in Umm Kulthum's \"Alf Leila w Leila\"."
  ],
  "text": "Iqa‘ Hacha‘ 4/4 (also in 2/4 and 6/4) Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Hacha‘ Iqa‘ Hacha‘ in 4/4 is very popular in Sufi music, especially in pieces that only use percussion instruments. Although the 4/4 version is by far the most prevalent, it is an adaptation of a more folkloric iqa‘ by the same name in 2/4. A rare adaptation is the 6/4 version used by composer Baligh Hamdi in Umm Kulthum's \"Alf Leila w Leila\". Bi-Hamdika Ya Ilahi Sheikh Hamza Shakkur & Ensemble Al Kindi Whirling Dervishes of Damascus Vol. 1 Subhana Sheikh Habboush & Ensemble Al Kindi Transe Soufie d'Aleppe Vol.2 il-Albi Yi‘shaq Kulli Gamil (1961) Umm Kulthum Music by Riyad al-Sunbati Qari'at al-Fingan (1976) Abdel Halim Hafez Music by Muhammad al-Mugi Qasida Qul Lil-Maliha Sabah Fakhri Tala‘a al-Badru ‘Alayna Hassan al-Haffar Iqa‘ Hacha‘ 4/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan Examples of the 2/4 form of Iqa‘ Hacha‘ ‘Al-Maya Diyab Mashhur (Syrian Folk Song) Iqa‘ Hacha‘ 2/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan Examples of the 6/4 form of Iqa‘ Hacha‘ Alf Leila w leila (1969) Umm Kulthum Music by Baligh Hamdi (Egypt) Iqa‘ Hacha‘ 6/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan",
